-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division B -- THE DIVISION OF UNADJUSTED PENSIONABLE EARNINGS
-- (sections 55, 55.1, 55.11 and 55.2(1) to (5.1)).
--
-- When spouses divorce or separate, or common-law partners separate, the pensionable earnings each earned during the time they
-- lived together can be pooled and split equally. Section 55 does it for divorces and annulments between 1978 and 1987, on
-- application; section 55.1, from 1987, does it on a divorce automatically and on separation on application, and covers
-- common-law partners. Section 55.11 says which cases section 55.1 reaches. Section 55.2 says that an agreement does not bind the
-- Minister (unless it expressly says there is to be no division), that the Minister must tell the persons, and how the earnings are
-- split. Section 55.2(5.2) onward is piece cp4.
--
-- Judgments the Act leaves to the Minister (approval of an application, being satisfied that a separation would have continued)
-- are plain inputs, supplied conditionally. Months of cohabitation "determined in the prescribed manner" are regulations 78 and 78.1
-- (piece cr2): an input. The period of a person's earnings "determined in the same manner as in section 78" is piece cp5: an input.
-- The words "coming into force of this section" in section 55.11 have no date in the text: the date is a stated input.

§ `Part II -- Division B -- the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (sections 55 to 55.2)`

§§ `Helpers of this module (no provision licenses them)`

-- Not a provision: the first day of 1978 and of 1987, the dates between which a judgment must have been rendered for section 55.
-- src:1498 | 55 (1) Subject to this section, subsections 55.2(2), (3) and (4) and section 55.3, an application for a division of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of former spouses may be made in writing to the Minister by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either former spouse or by any person that may be prescribed, within 36 months or, if both former spouses agree in writing, at any time after the date of a judgment granting a divorce or of a judgment of nullity of the marriage, rendered on or after January 1, 1978 and before January 1, 1987.
@ref Act s 55(1) (src:1498)
`s 55(1) — the first day of 1978, the earliest judgment` MEANS YearMonthDay 1978 1 1

-- src:1498 | 55 (1) Subject to this section, subsections 55.2(2), (3) and (4) and section 55.3, an application for a division of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of former spouses may be made in writing to the Minister by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either former spouse or by any person that may be prescribed, within 36 months or, if both former spouses agree in writing, at any time after the date of a judgment granting a divorce or of a judgment of nullity of the marriage, rendered on or after January 1, 1978 and before January 1, 1987.
@ref Act s 55(1) (src:1498)
`s 55(1) — the first day of 1987, the end of the judgments` MEANS YearMonthDay 1987 1 1

§§ `55 -- divorces and annulments between 1978 and 1987`

-- src:1498 | 55 (1) Subject to this section, subsections 55.2(2), (3) and (4) and section 55.3, an application for a division of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of former spouses may be made in writing to the Minister by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either former spouse or by any person that may be prescribed, within 36 months or, if both former spouses agree in writing, at any time after the date of a judgment granting a divorce or of a judgment of nullity of the marriage, rendered on or after January 1, 1978 and before January 1, 1987.
@ref Act s 55(1) (src:1498)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `both former spouses agree in writing that the application may be made at any time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: an application for a division of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of former spouses may be made, in writing to the Minister, by either
-- former spouse (or someone on their behalf), by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed, within 36 months after the date of a
-- judgment of divorce or nullity rendered from 1 January 1978 up to 1 January 1987, or, if both former spouses agree in writing, at any time after it. This is
-- the right to apply; the rest of Part II and sections 55.2(2) to (4) and 55.3 (piece cp4) qualify it.
-- out of range: section 55.3 (piece cp4), to which the subsection is "subject"; and regulations under subsection (9), which is inert.
`s 55(1) — an application for a division of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of former spouses may be made` `the application is made in writing to the Minister` `the application is made by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed` `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` `the day the application is made` `both former spouses agree in writing that the application may be made at any time` MEANS
        `the application is made in writing to the Minister`
    AND `the application is made by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed`
    AND `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` AT LEAST `s 55(1) — the first day of 1978, the earliest judgment`
    AND `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` LESS THAN `s 55(1) — the first day of 1987, the end of the judgments`
    AND (   `the day the application is made` AT LEAST `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date` `the day the application is made` `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 36)
         OR (    `both former spouses agree in writing that the application may be made at any time`
             AND `the day the application is made` AT LEAST `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage`))

-- src:1500 | (2) For the purposes of this section,
-- src:1501 | (a) notwithstanding paragraphs (b) and (c), the former spouses must have cohabited for at least thirty-six consecutive months during the marriage before an application made under subsection (1) may be approved by the Minister;
@ref Act s 55(2), (2)(a) (src:1500-1501)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive months during the marriage that the former spouses cohabited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: before the Minister may approve an application, the former spouses must have cohabited for at least 36 consecutive months during the marriage,
-- notwithstanding paragraphs (b) and (c).
`s 55(2)(a) — the former spouses cohabited for at least thirty-six consecutive months during the marriage` `the number of consecutive months during the marriage that the former spouses cohabited` MEANS
    `the number of consecutive months during the marriage that the former spouses cohabited` AT LEAST 36

-- src:1502 | (b) the marriage is deemed to have been solemnized or nullified or a divorce is deemed to have been made final on the last day of the year preceding the registered date of the marriage or the judgment of nullity or the effective date of the judgment granting a divorce; and
@ref Act s 55(2)(b) (src:1502)
GIVEN `the registered date of the marriage, or the registered date of the judgment of nullity, or the effective date of the judgment granting a divorce` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
-- Plain gloss: for this section the marriage is deemed solemnized, or nullified, or the divorce made final, on the last day of the year before the year
-- of the registered date of the marriage, the judgment of nullity or the effective date of the divorce.
`s 55(2)(b) — the day on which the marriage is deemed solemnized or nullified or a divorce is deemed made final` `the registered date of the marriage, or the registered date of the judgment of nullity, or the effective date of the judgment granting a divorce` MEANS
    YearMonthDay ((DATE_YEAR `the registered date of the marriage, or the registered date of the judgment of nullity, or the effective date of the judgment granting a divorce`) MINUS 1) 12 31

-- src:1503 | (c) the former spouses shall be deemed to have cohabited throughout the year in which the marriage was solemnized, and shall be deemed not to have cohabited at any time during the year of divorce or of annulment of the marriage.
@ref Act s 55(2)(c) (src:1503)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the year in which the marriage was solemnized` IS A NUMBER
      `the year of the divorce or of the annulment of the marriage` IS A NUMBER
      `the former spouses actually cohabited during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the former spouses are deemed to have cohabited throughout the year in which the marriage was solemnized, and deemed not to have cohabited at any time
-- during the year of divorce or annulment; in every other year they cohabited if they did. The years in question are the actual years, not the years of the deemed dates of
-- paragraph (b) (NOTES.md, fork register).
`s 55(2)(c) — the former spouses are deemed to have cohabited during a year` year `the year in which the marriage was solemnized` `the year of the divorce or of the annulment of the marriage` `the former spouses actually cohabited during the year` MEANS
    IF year EQUALS `the year of the divorce or of the annulment of the marriage`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF year EQUALS `the year in which the marriage was solemnized`
         THEN TRUE
         ELSE `the former spouses actually cohabited during the year`

-- src:1505 | (3) In determining the period for which the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the former spouses shall be divided, only those months during which the former spouses cohabited during the marriage shall be considered and, for the purposes of this section, months during which former spouses cohabited shall be determined in the prescribed manner.
@ref Act s 55(3) (src:1505)
GIVEN `the months of the marriage` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the months during which the former spouses cohabited during the marriage, determined in the prescribed manner` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
-- Plain gloss: in working out the period for which earnings are divided, only the months in which the former spouses cohabited during the marriage count, and which
-- months those are is determined in the prescribed manner (regulation 78, piece cr2), which is an input.
-- out of range: regulation 78 (piece cr2), the "prescribed manner" of determining months of cohabitation: taken as a list of months.
`s 55(3) — the months considered in determining the period for which the earnings are divided` `the months of the marriage` `the months during which the former spouses cohabited during the marriage, determined in the prescribed manner` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN month YIELD any (GIVEN m YIELD `the month of a date` m EQUALS `the month of a date` month) `the months during which the former spouses cohabited during the marriage, determined in the prescribed manner`) `the months of the marriage`

-- src:1507 | (4) On approval by the Minister of an application referred to in subsection (1), the unadjusted pensionable earnings for each former spouse for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under this Act, determined in the same manner as the total pensionable earnings attributable to contributions made under this Act are determined in section 78, shall be added and then divided equally and the unadjusted pensionable earnings so divided shall be attributed to each former spouse.
@ref Act s 55(4) (src:1507)
GIVEN `the Minister has approved the application referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first former spouse for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second former spouse for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: on the Minister's approval of the application, the unadjusted pensionable earnings of each former spouse for the period of cohabitation attributable to
-- contributions under this Act (worked out as section 78, piece cp5, works them out) are added and divided equally, and each former spouse is attributed half.
-- NOTHING means the Minister has not approved: no division is made.
-- out of range: section 78 (piece cp5): the earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions are taken as numbers.
`s 55(4) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each former spouse on a division` `the Minister has approved the application referred to in subsection (1)` `the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first former spouse for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under this Act` `the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second former spouse for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under this Act` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has approved the application referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST ((`the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first former spouse for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under this Act` PLUS `the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second former spouse for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under this Act`) DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1509 | (5) Where there is a division under subsection (4) and under a provincial pension plan, for the purposes of benefit calculation and payment under this Act, the total unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division shall be the aggregate of his unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (4) and his unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 55(5) (src:1509)
GIVEN `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
      `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: where there is a division under subsection (4) and under a provincial pension plan, the contributor's total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of
-- division, for benefits under this Act, are the earnings attributed under subsection (4) plus those attributed under the provincial plan.
`s 55(5) — the total unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division under this Act and a provincial pension plan` `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (4)` `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan` MEANS
    `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (4)` PLUS `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan`

-- src:1511 | (6) No division of unadjusted pensionable earnings for a period of cohabitation shall be made
-- src:1512 | (a) where the total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the former spouses in a year does not exceed twice the Year’s Basic Exemption;
-- src:1513 | (b) for the period before which one of the former spouses reached eighteen years of age or after which a former spouse reached seventy years of age;
-- src:1514 | (c) for the period in which one of the former spouses was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan; and
-- src:1515 | (d) for any month that is excluded from the contributory period of one of the former spouses under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability.
@ref Act s 55(6) (src:1511-1515)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the former spouses in the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the first former spouse's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the second former spouse's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the first former spouse was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second former spouse was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month is excluded from the contributory period of the first former spouse under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month is excluded from the contributory period of the second former spouse under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a division is made for a month of the period of cohabitation unless (a) the former spouses' total earnings in the year do not exceed twice the Year's Basic
-- Exemption, (b) the month is before one of them reached 18 or after one reached 70 (section 2(2)'s deemed dates), (c) one of them was a beneficiary of a retirement pension then, or
-- (d) the month is excluded from the contributory period of one of them by reason of disability.
`s 55(6) — a division is made for a month of the period of cohabitation` month `the total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the former spouses in the year` `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the first former spouse's date of birth` `the second former spouse's date of birth` `the first former spouse was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` `the second former spouse was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` `the month is excluded from the contributory period of the first former spouse under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` `the month is excluded from the contributory period of the second former spouse under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` MEANS
        (NOT (`the total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the former spouses in the year` AT MOST (2 TIMES `the Year's Basic Exemption`)))
    AND (NOT (`before the 18th or after the 70th`))
    AND (NOT (   `the first former spouse was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month`
              OR `the second former spouse was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month`))
    AND (NOT (   `the month is excluded from the contributory period of the first former spouse under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability`
              OR `the month is excluded from the contributory period of the second former spouse under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability`))
    WHERE
        `the month of reaching` born age MEANS `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` born age)
        `before the 18th or after the 70th` MEANS
               `the month of a date` month LESS THAN `the month of reaching` `the first former spouse's date of birth` 18
            OR `the month of a date` month LESS THAN `the month of reaching` `the second former spouse's date of birth` 18
            OR `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `the month of reaching` `the first former spouse's date of birth` 70
            OR `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `the month of reaching` `the second former spouse's date of birth` 70

-- src:1517 | (7) Where an application referred to in subsection (1) has been approved and a benefit is payable under this Act to or in respect of either of the former spouses for any month commencing on or before the day of receipt of an application under subsection (1), the basic amount of the benefit shall be calculated and adjusted in accordance with section 45 but subject to the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings made under this section and the adjusted benefit shall be paid effective the month following the month the application referred to in subsection (1) is received.
@ref Act s 55(7) (src:1517)
GIVEN `the application referred to in subsection (1) has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit is payable under this Act to or in respect of either of the former spouses for a month commencing on or before the day of receipt of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
-- Plain gloss: where an approved application finds a benefit already payable for a month on or before the day the application was received, the benefit is recalculated
-- and adjusted under section 45 subject to the division, and the adjusted benefit is paid from the month after the month the application was received. The result is
-- that month. NOTHING means the subsection does not apply.
`s 55(7) — the month from which the benefit adjusted for the division is paid` `the application referred to in subsection (1) has been approved` `a benefit is payable under this Act to or in respect of either of the former spouses for a month commencing on or before the day of receipt of the application` `the day the application was received` MEANS
    IF `the application referred to in subsection (1) has been approved` AND `a benefit is payable under this Act to or in respect of either of the former spouses for a month commencing on or before the day of receipt of the application`
    THEN JUST (`the month following the month of a date` `the day the application was received`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1519 | (8) On approval by the Minister of an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings, an applicant and the former spouse or the former spouse’s estate shall be notified in a manner prescribed by regulation and, where the applicant or the former spouse or the former spouse’s estate is dissatisfied with the division or the result thereof, the right of appeal as set out in this Part applies.
@ref Act s 55(8) (src:1519)
GIVEN `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: on approval of an application, the applicant and the former spouse or the former spouse's estate must be notified, in the manner prescribed by regulation.
-- This is a duty of the Minister to give notice; the person notified is owed it.
-- out of range: the manner of notice "prescribed by regulation" (the Regulations, Part V: piece cr2).
`s 55(8) — the applicant and the former spouse or the former spouse's estate must be notified of the approval` `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` MEANS
    `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings`

-- src:1519 | (8) On approval by the Minister of an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings, an applicant and the former spouse or the former spouse’s estate shall be notified in a manner prescribed by regulation and, where the applicant or the former spouse or the former spouse’s estate is dissatisfied with the division or the result thereof, the right of appeal as set out in this Part applies.
@ref Act s 55(8) (src:1519)
GIVEN `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant, or the former spouse or the former spouse's estate, is dissatisfied with the division or the result of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: an applicant, or the former spouse or the former spouse's estate, who is dissatisfied with the division or its result has the right of appeal that Part II
-- provides (Divisions F and following: pieces cp4 and cp5).
-- out of range: the right of appeal "as set out in this Part" (reconsiderations and appeals, piece cp5).
`s 55(8) — an applicant or a former spouse who is dissatisfied with the division has the right of appeal` `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` `the applicant, or the former spouse or the former spouse's estate, is dissatisfied with the division or the result of it` MEANS
    `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` AND `the applicant, or the former spouse or the former spouse's estate, is dissatisfied with the division or the result of it`

§§ `55.1 -- the division on a divorce, a separation or the end of a common-law partnership`

-- src:1526 | (a) in the case of spouses, following a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage, on the Minister’s being informed of the judgment and receiving the prescribed information;
@ref Act s 55.1(1)(a) (src:1526)
GIVEN `a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage has been given in the case of spouses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has been informed of the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has received the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: spouses whose marriage is ended by a judgment of divorce or nullity have their earnings divided as soon as the Minister is informed of the judgment and has the
-- prescribed information: no application is needed.
`s 55.1(1)(a) — a division takes place on a judgment granting a divorce or of nullity of the marriage` `a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage has been given in the case of spouses` `the Minister has been informed of the judgment` `the Minister has received the prescribed information` MEANS
    `a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage has been given in the case of spouses` AND `the Minister has been informed of the judgment` AND `the Minister has received the prescribed information`

-- src:1527 | (b) in the case of spouses, following the approval by the Minister of an application made by or on behalf of either spouse, by the estate or succession of either spouse or by any person that may be prescribed, if
-- src:1528 | (i) the spouses have been living separate and apart for a period of one year or more, and
-- src:1529 | (ii) in the event of the death of one of the spouses after they have been living separate and apart for a period of one year or more, the application is made within three years after the death; and
@ref Act s 55.1(1)(b) (src:1527-1529)
GIVEN `the persons are spouses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the spouses commenced to live separate and apart` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day one of the spouses died, if one died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: spouses have their earnings divided on the Minister's approval of an application, if they have been living separate and apart for a year or more (counted to the
-- death where one has died), and, where one of them died after they had lived apart for a year or more, the application is made within three years after the death.
-- A death before the year of separation is complete leaves limb (i) unmet. The three-year limit is only for the case of a death (fork F19).
`s 55.1(1)(b) — a division takes place on the approval of an application by spouses living separate and apart` `the persons are spouses` `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed` `the day the spouses commenced to live separate and apart` `the day the application is made` `the day one of the spouses died, if one died` MEANS
        `the persons are spouses`
    AND `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed`
    AND `limb (i)`
    AND `limb (ii)`
    WHERE
        `the day the year of separation is tested` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day one of the spouses died, if one died`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the application is made`
            WHEN JUST died THEN died
        `limb (i)` MEANS `the date a time limit ends` `the day the spouses commenced to live separate and apart` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1) AT MOST `the day the year of separation is tested`
        `limb (ii)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day one of the spouses died, if one died`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST died THEN `the day the application is made` AT MOST `the date a time limit ends` died (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 3)

-- src:1530 | (c) in the case of common-law partners, following the approval by the Minister of an application made by or on behalf of either former common-law partner, by the estate or succession of one of those former common-law partners or by any person that may be prescribed, if
-- src:1531 | (i) the former common-law partners have been living separate and apart for a period of one year or more, or one of the former common-law partners has died during that period, and
-- src:1532 | (ii) the application is made within four years after the day on which the former common-law partners commenced to live separate and apart or, if both former common-law partners agree in writing, at any time after the end of that four-year period.
@ref Act s 55.1(1)(c) (src:1530-1532)
GIVEN `the persons are former common-law partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either former common-law partner, by the estate or succession of one of them, or by a person who may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the former common-law partners commenced to live separate and apart` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day one of the former common-law partners died during the period of living separate and apart, if one did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `both former common-law partners agree in writing to an application made at any time after the end of the four-year period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: former common-law partners have their earnings divided on the Minister's approval of an application, if they have been living separate and apart for a year or more
-- (or one has died during that period) and the application is made within four years after they commenced to live apart or, if both agree in writing, at any time after those four years.
`s 55.1(1)(c) — a division takes place on the approval of an application by former common-law partners living separate and apart` `the persons are former common-law partners` `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either former common-law partner, by the estate or succession of one of them, or by a person who may be prescribed` `the day the former common-law partners commenced to live separate and apart` `the day the application is made` `the day one of the former common-law partners died during the period of living separate and apart, if one did` `both former common-law partners agree in writing to an application made at any time after the end of the four-year period` MEANS
        `the persons are former common-law partners`
    AND `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either former common-law partner, by the estate or succession of one of them, or by a person who may be prescribed`
    AND `limb (i)`
    AND `limb (ii)`
    WHERE
        `limb (i)` MEANS
            (`the date a time limit ends` `the day the former common-law partners commenced to live separate and apart` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1) AT MOST `the day the application is made`)
            OR (CONSIDER `the day one of the former common-law partners died during the period of living separate and apart, if one did`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                WHEN JUST died THEN TRUE)
        `limb (ii)` MEANS
                `the day the application is made` AT MOST `the date a time limit ends` `the day the former common-law partners commenced to live separate and apart` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 4)
            OR `both former common-law partners agree in writing to an application made at any time after the end of the four-year period`

-- src:1534 | (2) For the purposes of this section,
-- src:1535 | (a) persons subject to a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings shall be deemed to have lived separate and apart for any period during which they lived apart and either of them had the intention to live separate and apart from the other; and
@ref Act s 55.1(2)(a) (src:1534-1535)
GIVEN `the persons lived apart during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `either of them had the intention to live separate and apart from the other during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.1(2)(a) — the persons are deemed to have lived separate and apart for a period` `the persons lived apart during the period` `either of them had the intention to live separate and apart from the other during the period` MEANS
    `the persons lived apart during the period` AND `either of them had the intention to live separate and apart from the other during the period`

-- src:1536 | (b) a period during which persons subject to such a division have lived separate and apart shall not be considered to have been interrupted or terminated
-- src:1537 | (i) by reason only that either person has become incapable of forming or having an intention to continue to live separate and apart or of continuing to live separate and apart of the person’s own volition, if it appears to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued if the person had not become so incapable, or
-- src:1538 | (ii) by reason only that the two persons have resumed cohabitation during a period of, or periods totalling, not more than ninety days with reconciliation as its primary purpose.
@ref Act s 55.1(2)(b) (src:1536-1538)
GIVEN `the only reason for the interruption is that either person has become incapable of forming or having an intention to continue to live separate and apart or of continuing to live separate and apart of the person's own volition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued if the person had not become so incapable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason for the interruption is that the two persons have resumed cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days of resumed cohabitation, in total` IS A NUMBER
      `reconciliation was the primary purpose of the resumed cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a period of living separate and apart is not considered interrupted or ended (i) by reason only that either person has become incapable of forming or keeping the
-- intention or of continuing apart of their own volition, if it appears to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued, or (ii) by reason only that the two
-- resumed cohabitation for a period or periods totalling not more than ninety days with reconciliation as its primary purpose.
`s 55.1(2)(b) — a period of living separate and apart is not considered to have been interrupted or terminated` `the only reason for the interruption is that either person has become incapable of forming or having an intention to continue to live separate and apart or of continuing to live separate and apart of the person's own volition` `it appears to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued if the person had not become so incapable` `the only reason for the interruption is that the two persons have resumed cohabitation` `the days of resumed cohabitation, in total` `reconciliation was the primary purpose of the resumed cohabitation` MEANS
        (`the only reason for the interruption is that either person has become incapable of forming or having an intention to continue to live separate and apart or of continuing to live separate and apart of the person's own volition` AND `it appears to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued if the person had not become so incapable`)
    OR  (`the only reason for the interruption is that the two persons have resumed cohabitation` AND `the days of resumed cohabitation, in total` AT MOST 90 AND `reconciliation was the primary purpose of the resumed cohabitation`)

-- src:1540 | (3) For the purposes of this section, persons subject to a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings must have cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year in order for the division to take place, and, for the purposes of this subsection, a continuous period of at least one year shall be determined in a manner prescribed by regulation.
@ref Act s 55.1(3) (src:1540)
GIVEN `the persons cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year, determined in a manner prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: for a division to take place the persons must have cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year; how a continuous year is determined is left to a
-- regulation (regulation 78.1, piece cr2), so whether they did is a plain input.
-- out of range: regulation 78.1(2) (piece cr2), the manner prescribed for determining the continuous year: taken as a fact.
`s 55.1(3) — the persons subject to a division cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year` `the persons cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year, determined in a manner prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    `the persons cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year, determined in a manner prescribed by regulation`

-- src:1542 | (4) In determining the period for which the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons subject to a division shall be divided, only those months during which the two persons cohabited shall be considered, and, for the purposes of this subsection, months during which the two persons cohabited shall be determined in the prescribed manner.
@ref Act s 55.1(4) (src:1542)
GIVEN `the months of the period of cohabitation` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the months during which the two persons cohabited, determined in the prescribed manner` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
-- out of range: regulation 78.1(1) (piece cr2), the "prescribed manner" of determining months of cohabitation: taken as a list of months.
`s 55.1(4) — the months considered in determining the period for which the earnings are divided` `the months of the period of cohabitation` `the months during which the two persons cohabited, determined in the prescribed manner` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN month YIELD any (GIVEN m YIELD `the month of a date` m EQUALS `the month of a date` month) `the months during which the two persons cohabited, determined in the prescribed manner`) `the months of the period of cohabitation`

-- src:1544 | (5) Before a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is made under this section, or within the prescribed period after such a division is made, the Minister may refuse to make the division or may cancel the division, as the case may be, if the Minister is satisfied that
-- src:1545 | (a) benefits are payable to or in respect of both persons subject to the division; and
-- src:1546 | (b) the amount of both benefits decreased at the time the division was made or would decrease at the time the division was proposed to be made.
@ref Act s 55.1(5) (src:1544-1546)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that benefits are payable to or in respect of both persons subject to the division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the amount of both benefits decreased at the time the division was made or would decrease at the time the division was proposed to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the division has not yet been made, or it was made within the prescribed period before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: before a division is made, or within the prescribed period after it, the Minister may refuse to make it or may cancel it if the Minister is satisfied that
-- benefits are payable to or in respect of both persons and that the amount of both benefits decreased (or would decrease) at the time of the division. The rule says whether
-- the Minister has that power; whether the Minister uses it is not decided. For the persons it is what may be done to them.
`s 55.1(5) — the Minister may refuse to make or may cancel a division` `the Minister is satisfied that benefits are payable to or in respect of both persons subject to the division` `the Minister is satisfied that the amount of both benefits decreased at the time the division was made or would decrease at the time the division was proposed to be made` `the division has not yet been made, or it was made within the prescribed period before` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that benefits are payable to or in respect of both persons subject to the division`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the amount of both benefits decreased at the time the division was made or would decrease at the time the division was proposed to be made`
    AND `the division has not yet been made, or it was made within the prescribed period before`

-- src:1523 | Division of Unadjusted Pensionable Earnings
-- src:1524 | When mandatory division to take place
-- src:1525 | 55.1 (1) Subject to this section and sections 55.2 and 55.3, a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings shall take place in the following circumstances:
-- src:1526 | (a) in the case of spouses, following a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage, on the Minister’s being informed of the judgment and receiving the prescribed information;
-- src:1527 | (b) in the case of spouses, following the approval by the Minister of an application made by or on behalf of either spouse, by the estate or succession of either spouse or by any person that may be prescribed, if
-- src:1528 | (i) the spouses have been living separate and apart for a period of one year or more, and
-- src:1529 | (ii) in the event of the death of one of the spouses after they have been living separate and apart for a period of one year or more, the application is made within three years after the death; and
-- src:1530 | (c) in the case of common-law partners, following the approval by the Minister of an application made by or on behalf of either former common-law partner, by the estate or succession of one of those former common-law partners or by any person that may be prescribed, if
-- src:1531 | (i) the former common-law partners have been living separate and apart for a period of one year or more, or one of the former common-law partners has died during that period, and
-- src:1532 | (ii) the application is made within four years after the day on which the former common-law partners commenced to live separate and apart or, if both former common-law partners agree in writing, at any time after the end of that four-year period.
-- src:1533 | Calculation of period of separation
-- src:1534 | (2) For the purposes of this section,
-- src:1535 | (a) persons subject to a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings shall be deemed to have lived separate and apart for any period during which they lived apart and either of them had the intention to live separate and apart from the other; and
-- src:1536 | (b) a period during which persons subject to such a division have lived separate and apart shall not be considered to have been interrupted or terminated
-- src:1537 | (i) by reason only that either person has become incapable of forming or having an intention to continue to live separate and apart or of continuing to live separate and apart of the person’s own volition, if it appears to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued if the person had not become so incapable, or
-- src:1538 | (ii) by reason only that the two persons have resumed cohabitation during a period of, or periods totalling, not more than ninety days with reconciliation as its primary purpose.
-- src:1539 | Period of cohabitation
-- src:1540 | (3) For the purposes of this section, persons subject to a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings must have cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year in order for the division to take place, and, for the purposes of this subsection, a continuous period of at least one year shall be determined in a manner prescribed by regulation.
-- src:1541 | Period for purposes of division
-- src:1542 | (4) In determining the period for which the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons subject to a division shall be divided, only those months during which the two persons cohabited shall be considered, and, for the purposes of this subsection, months during which the two persons cohabited shall be determined in the prescribed manner.
-- src:1543 | Minister’s discretion
-- src:1544 | (5) Before a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is made under this section, or within the prescribed period after such a division is made, the Minister may refuse to make the division or may cancel the division, as the case may be, if the Minister is satisfied that
-- src:1545 | (a) benefits are payable to or in respect of both persons subject to the division; and
-- src:1546 | (b) the amount of both benefits decreased at the time the division was made or would decrease at the time the division was proposed to be made.
@ref Act s 55.1 (src:1523-1546)
GIVEN `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons subject to the division cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written agreement binds the Minister under subsection 55.2(3), so that the Minister shall not make a division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has refused to make or has cancelled the division under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place under section 55.1 if one of paragraphs (1)(a), (b) and (c) is met, the persons cohabited for a continuous year
-- (subsection (3)), no agreement binds the Minister (subsection 55.2(3)) and the Minister has not refused or cancelled it (subsection (5)). The section is "subject to" those and to section 55.3 (piece cp4).
-- out of range: section 55.3 (piece cp4), to which the subsection is "subject".
`s 55.1 — a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place` `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(a)` `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(b)` `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(c)` `the persons subject to the division cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year` `a written agreement binds the Minister under subsection 55.2(3), so that the Minister shall not make a division` `the Minister has refused to make or has cancelled the division under subsection (5)` MEANS
        (`a division takes place under paragraph (1)(a)` OR `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(b)` OR `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(c)`)
    AND `the persons subject to the division cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year`
    AND (NOT `a written agreement binds the Minister under subsection 55.2(3), so that the Minister shall not make a division`)
    AND (NOT `the Minister has refused to make or has cancelled the division under subsection (5)`)

§§ `55.11 -- the cases section 55.1 applies to`

-- src:1548 | 55.11 Section 55.1 applies
-- src:1549 | (a) in respect of judgments granting a divorce and judgments of nullity of a marriage, rendered on or after January 1, 1987;
-- src:1550 | (b) in respect of spouses and former spouses who commence to live separate and apart on or after January 1, 1987 but before the coming into force of this section (spouse having in this paragraph the meaning that it had immediately before that coming into force); and
-- src:1551 | (c) in respect of spouses and former common-law partners who commence to live separate and apart after the coming into force of this section.
@ref Act s 55.11 (src:1548-1551)
GIVEN `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the persons commenced to live separate and apart, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the persons are spouses or former spouses, spouse having the meaning it had immediately before the coming into force of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons are spouses or former common-law partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day section 55.11 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: section 55.1 applies (a) to judgments of divorce or nullity rendered on or after 1 January 1987; (b) to spouses and former spouses who commence to live separate and apart on or
-- after 1 January 1987 but before this section came into force (spouse in the sense it had before that); (c) to spouses and former common-law partners who commence to live separate and
-- apart after this section came into force. The text gives no date for the coming into force: it is a stated input. "Spouse" as it then stood was defined in section 2(1), now repealed.
`s 55.11 — section 55.1 applies to the case` `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage, if there was one` `the day the persons commenced to live separate and apart, if they did` `the persons are spouses or former spouses, spouse having the meaning it had immediately before the coming into force of this section` `the persons are spouses or former common-law partners` `the day section 55.11 came into force` MEANS
        `paragraph (a)`
    OR  `paragraph (b)`
    OR  `paragraph (c)`
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage, if there was one`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST judged THEN judged AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the persons are spouses or former spouses, spouse having the meaning it had immediately before the coming into force of this section`
            AND (CONSIDER `the day the persons commenced to live separate and apart, if they did`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                 WHEN JUST apart THEN apart AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) AND apart LESS THAN `the day section 55.11 came into force`)
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            `the persons are spouses or former common-law partners`
            AND (CONSIDER `the day the persons commenced to live separate and apart, if they did`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                 WHEN JUST apart THEN apart GREATER THAN `the day section 55.11 came into force`)

§§ `55.2 -- agreements, notice and the split`

-- src:1554 | (2) Except as provided in subsection (3), where, on or after June 4, 1986, a written agreement between persons subject to a division under section 55 or 55.1 was entered into, or a court order was made, the provisions of that agreement or court order are not binding on the Minister for the purposes of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1.
@ref Act s 55.2(2) (src:1554)
GIVEN `a written agreement between persons subject to a division under section 55 or 55.1 was entered into, or a court order was made, on or after June 4, 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (3) makes the provision of the agreement binding on the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the provisions of a written agreement between the persons, or of a court order, made on or after 4 June 1986 do not bind the Minister in a division under section 55
-- or 55.1, except as subsection (3) provides. The dates of the agreement and the order are the first input's.
`s 55.2(2) — an agreement or court order does not bind the Minister in a division` `a written agreement between persons subject to a division under section 55 or 55.1 was entered into, or a court order was made, on or after June 4, 1986` `subsection (3) makes the provision of the agreement binding on the Minister` MEANS
    `a written agreement between persons subject to a division under section 55 or 55.1 was entered into, or a court order was made, on or after June 4, 1986` AND (NOT `subsection (3) makes the provision of the agreement binding on the Minister`)

-- src:1556 | (3) Where
-- src:1557 | (a) a written agreement between persons subject to a division under section 55 or 55.1 entered into on or after June 4, 1986 contains a provision that expressly mentions this Act and indicates the intention of the persons that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1,
-- src:1558 | (b) that provision of the agreement is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements,
-- src:1559 | (c) the agreement was entered into
-- src:1560 | (i) in the case of a division under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c), before the day of the application for the division, or
-- src:1561 | (ii) in the case of a division under paragraph 55.1(1)(a), before the rendering of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage, as the case may be, and
-- src:1562 | (d) that provision of the agreement has not been invalidated by a court order,
-- src:1563 | that provision of the agreement is binding on the Minister and, consequently, the Minister shall not make a division under section 55 or 55.1.
@ref Act s 55.2(3) (src:1556-1563)
GIVEN `a written agreement between persons subject to a division was entered into on or after June 4, 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement contains a provision that expressly mentions this Act and indicates the intention of the persons that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that provision is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the division is under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the division is under paragraph 55.1(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the agreement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application for the division` IS A DATE
      `the day of the rendering of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` IS A DATE
      `that provision has not been invalidated by a court order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a provision of a written agreement made on or after 4 June 1986 that expressly mentions the Act and says there is to be no division is binding on the Minister, and the Minister
-- shall not make a division, if the provincial law expressly permits it, it was made before the application (for a division under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)) or before the
-- judgment (for a division under paragraph 55.1(1)(a)), and no court order has invalidated it. All of paragraphs (a) to (d) are needed: the text joins them with "and".
`s 55.2(3) — a provision of an agreement is binding on the Minister and the Minister shall not make a division` `a written agreement between persons subject to a division was entered into on or after June 4, 1986` `the agreement contains a provision that expressly mentions this Act and indicates the intention of the persons that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` `that provision is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements` `the division is under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)` `the division is under paragraph 55.1(1)(a)` `the day the agreement was entered into` `the day of the application for the division` `the day of the rendering of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` `that provision has not been invalidated by a court order` MEANS
        `a written agreement between persons subject to a division was entered into on or after June 4, 1986`
    AND `the agreement contains a provision that expressly mentions this Act and indicates the intention of the persons that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1`
    AND `that provision is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements`
    AND (   (`the division is under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)` AND `the day the agreement was entered into` LESS THAN `the day of the application for the division`)
         OR (`the division is under paragraph 55.1(1)(a)` AND `the day the agreement was entered into` LESS THAN `the day of the rendering of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage`))
    AND `that provision has not been invalidated by a court order`

-- src:1565 | (4) The Minister shall, without delay after being informed of a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of a marriage or after receiving an application under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c), notify each of the persons subject to the division, in the prescribed manner, of the periods of unadjusted pensionable earnings to be divided, and of any other information that the Minister considers necessary.
@ref Act s 55.2(4) (src:1565)
GIVEN `the Minister has been informed of a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has received an application under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the Minister shall, without delay after being informed of a judgment of divorce or nullity or receiving an application, notify each person subject to the division, in the prescribed manner, of
-- the periods of unadjusted pensionable earnings to be divided and of any other information the Minister considers necessary. The rule says whether each person is owed that notice.
-- out of range: regulation 46 (piece cr2), the manner of the notification.
`s 55.2(4) — each person subject to the division must be notified without delay` `the Minister has been informed of a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of a marriage` `the Minister has received an application under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)` MEANS
    `the Minister has been informed of a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of a marriage` OR `the Minister has received an application under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)`

-- src:1567 | (5) If there is a division under section 55.1, the base unadjusted pensionable earnings for each person subject to the division for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under this Act, determined in the same manner as the total pensionable earnings of a contributor attributable to base contributions made under this Act are determined in section 78, are to be added and then divided equally, and the base unadjusted pensionable earnings so divided are to be attributed to each person.
@ref Act s 55.2(5) (src:1567)
GIVEN `there is a division under section 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first person for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second person for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: if there is a division under section 55.1, the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of each person for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions (worked out as section 78,
-- piece cp5, works them out) are added and divided equally, and each person is attributed half. NOTHING means there is no division.
-- out of range: section 78 (piece cp5): the earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions are taken as numbers.
`s 55.2(5) — the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person on a division under section 55.1` `there is a division under section 55.1` `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first person for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under this Act` `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second person for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under this Act` MEANS
    IF `there is a division under section 55.1`
    THEN JUST ((`the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first person for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under this Act` PLUS `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second person for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under this Act`) DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1569 | (5.1) If there is a division under section 55.1, the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for each person subject to the division for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act, determined in the same manner as the total first additional pensionable earnings of a contributor attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act are determined in section 78.1, are to be added and then divided equally, and the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings so divided are to be attributed to each person.
@ref Act s 55.2(5.1) (src:1569)
GIVEN `there is a division under section 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first person for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second person for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the same for the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings (worked out as section 78.1, piece cp5).
-- out of range: section 78.1 (piece cp5): the earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions are taken as numbers.
`s 55.2(5.1) — the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person on a division under section 55.1` `there is a division under section 55.1` `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first person for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second person for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` MEANS
    IF `there is a division under section 55.1`
    THEN JUST ((`the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the first person for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` PLUS `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the second person for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act`) DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE NOTHING
